items.details:
Generated inside finalRelease() with no user click (AS-12) and stored frozen on the case (c.finalDocument). Shown as the Case 360 tab 'Final document' (or /cases/:id/document), with a Print button (window.print, print CSS).

Content (REQ-PROC-046 plus R-2):
- CIQ ID, material, supplier, manufacturer and site, target markets, template and rule-set versions;
- the released answers per in-scope section, incl. the K2.1 component table and justifications;
- the evidence list: file name, section and question, uploader, upload date (no attachments embedded);
- every open point's full thread in order: raised, edited, answered, returned, accepted or closed, each with who, when and the section/field reference;
- the three confirmation kinds: completeness, each review completion (RMM and departments), final release;
- the generation time.

It holds no internal notes, RMES results or findings. Internal roles see it read-only. The RMM owner gets an inbox mail linking to it. Before completion the tab is hidden.

Keep the reminders table. Notification events become:
- invitation (case created → selected supplier contacts);
- open point raised, edited, returned or closed (one generic mail → the supplier contacts of the case);
- open point answered (→ the raiser, plus the responsible person if different);
- final release (→ the RMM owner, with the link to the final document);
- cancellation (neutral notice → supplier contacts).

One reusable template, not one per flow. The previews become two static templates with placeholders (supplier version: neutral, no question text and no internal content; internal version: may quote the answer), plus a link 'See the Inbox'. Remove the 'live case data' hint.

Start state:
- every internal role holder: INTERNAL users at seed.ts:48-65, all fictional;
- ONE fictional supplier with its 2 contacts;
- templates v1 published and v2 draft, active RS-2026.1, default ownership, default reminders;
- cases: [] and mails: [].

Every internal screen must render with this state (TEST-02). Thomas creates the case in the demo.

Internal personas get /inbox; supplier contacts get the portal inbox (portal-side twin, same data).

**Layout:** a list (from, subject, case, time, unread dot) and a reading pane. The mail shows To, Subject and Body, and a 'Open <case / open point>' button that deep-links to the workspace or the case.

**Exactly one mail per event:**
- open point raised, edited, returned or closed → every supplier contact of the case;
- supplier answered (or cannot provide) → the raiser, plus the responsible person if different;
- case created → the invited contacts;
- final release → the RMM owner, with the final-document link;
- case cancelled → the supplier contacts.

**Content rule:** supplier mails never contain internal content (no reviewer comments, findings, RMES or department status). They name the material, case, reference and due date, and link to the portal.

**Empty state:** 'No mail yet'.

Internal screens must make it visible:
- the reopened track chip;
- the 'Added after completeness' section badge;
- the case moving back from 'Awaiting final release' to 'Review', with its audit row;
- an inbox mail to the newly activated or reopened department assignee (internal), so the reviewer knows why their queue changed.

Covered by tests.

A domain-level scenario test (vitest, pure actions) plus a browser harness:
- empty start;
- RMM adds a supplier (optional) and creates a case (invitation mail);
- the supplier answers metadata (sections open and close), fills in and confirms completeness;
- RMM and the activated departments get tasks;
- REG raises a point (supplier mail), edits it (mail), the supplier answers (mail to REG), REG returns (mail) or accepts;
- QM raises and closes a point (mail);
- SAF RMES with a rejection;
- every track completes, so the release request goes out;
- the supplier releases, so the case completes and the final document exists with every thread round and no attachments or internal notes;
- the RMM owner gets the final-document mail;
- Reports and Audit show the data.

Assert the nav of each persona equals the final list (NAV-02..07).

Render each route (/rmm, /cases, /cases/new, /review, /suppliers, /inbox, /reports, /audit, /admin/*) for each internal persona on the empty start. Assert:
- no crash;
- the defined empty-state copy;
- no text matching /0 days|0 %|Passed|0 reference materials|Longest internal queue/;
- no 'Review version' and no 'Our understanding'.

Cases to cover:
- editOpenPoint and closeOpenPoint: only the raiser; status and outcome; track status; the thread message; the audit row; exactly one mail each;
- mail generation for raise, answer, return, accept, close-not-accepted, invitation, cancel and final release (recipients, no internal content in supplier mails);
- finalDocument content: all sections, evidence by name and date, every thread round in order, the three confirmation kinds, no RMES or notes; immutable after creation;
- supplier master: unique DUNS, contact deactivation, personas derived from contacts;
- the regression reference set is independent of state.cases.

Move the existing seed and attention tests onto the rich fixture (LAY-03).
